WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.720
Tilda Swinton is an actor like no other, with
wide-ranging roles in films like "Doctor Strange"

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:06.720
and "Suspiria.”

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.360
It may have been a while since Swinton's last
big movie, but that doesn't mean she hasn't

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.559
been busy.

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:14.110
Here's why you may not have seen very much
of Swinton lately.

00:00:15.509 --> 00:00:18.939
When Swinton first began her acting career,
she moved to London to work with the Royal

00:00:18.939 --> 00:00:20.210
Shakespeare Company.

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:24.330
However, she moved back to her childhood home
of Scotland once she had grown tired of the

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.330
city life.

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:29.560
A small-town homebody at heart, she has made
a comfortable life for herself and her family

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.240
in the Scottish Highlands.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.090
As she said in an interview for Esquire,

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:36.280
"I mean, I've even lost the way of living
in a city.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:39.079
If I had to live in a city again, it would
take me a long time.

00:00:39.079 --> 00:00:41.550
You have to train up to live in a city."

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:45.430
Today, Swinton says that she rarely visits
London anymore and feels that she is "out

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:47.390
of touch" with the industry there.

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:51.730
Although she does occasionally think about
moving back to a city, she has no plans to

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:52.829
do so in the near future.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:57.640
Swinton has fans all around the world, but
she couldn't tell you what they are saying

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:02.340
about her online, thanks to her decision to
stay off social media entirely.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:06.690
The actor considers herself a, quote, "complete
Luddite," telling Vogue,

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:10.090
"I have no presence on social media, absolutely
none…

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:12.090
I just have other things to do.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.580
I know it's going on.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:17.860
It's like there's a forest on fire somewhere
down the end of the garden, but I'm concentrating

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:19.440
on the roses."

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:23.990
While Swinton's fans would probably love to
see her on Twitter or Instagram, it's unlikely

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:26.210
she'll be creating an account anytime soon.

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.210
"Application denied!

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.210
I'm sorry!"

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:34.350
Despite her bulky resume, Swinton insists
that she is not an ambitious person, saying,

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:37.180
"I've never had any ambition as an artist.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:40.530
That may sound crazy and transgressive, but
it's a fact,"

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:44.490
In fact, Swinton has admitted that she does
not even think of herself as a traditional

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:47.540
actress, even though she's been acting for
over 30 years.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.950
While she will certainly accept the opportunity
to appear in a blockbuster franchise when

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:56.450
the chance comes around, she isn't specifically
seeking out these roles.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:00.030
And Swinton doesn't go to auditions anymore,
either — she's accomplished enough that

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.750
directors come to her.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:05.250
Overall, she will always put passion over
potential profits.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:10.810
For Swinton, the director she's working with
is often more important than the film itself.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:15.571
She has worked at least three times each with
directors Wes Anderson, Jim Jarmusch, and

00:02:15.571 --> 00:02:17.290
Luca Guadagnino.

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:21.780
In the early years of her career, she worked
closely with director Derek Jarman on several

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:26.310
more experimental films, which taught her
that supportive relationships with directors

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:29.920
who shared her vision were the key to artistic
fulfillment.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.800
In an interview, Swinton told The Independent,

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:36.850
"We are used to actors moving from project
to project in a slightly detached way, or

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:40.690
that they are looking over their shoulder
for a more interesting project, or more money,

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:42.660
but that is not how I approach [it]…

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.100
I need to work with people that I can trust.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.990
I always choose the people first."

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:51.960
Swinton is far more likely to wait for an
intriguing role with the right director, even

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:55.310
if it means passing up roles that other actors
might have jumped at.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:00.650
Swinton knows that a great film can take time,
which is why she's willing to spend several

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:05.540
years patiently working to give a single project
the attention it deserves.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:10.080
Swinton states that this kind of focused,
long-term attention makes her process unique,

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.600
allowing her to personally develop her roles
alongside her directors and writers.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:15.720
She revealed to Variety,

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:20.360
"Most people don't develop work the way I
customarily do… they'll wait for someone

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:23.790
to place them into their universe with proper
crafts­people.

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:27.730
Whereas I spend most of my time sitting around
my kitchen table with friends, chewing on

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:31.100
ideas and building things that take years."

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:35.420
Swinton spent five years working on the film
"Orlando" with director Sally Potter, and

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:40.380
she dedicated, quote, "seven or eight years"
to "Only Lovers Left Alive."

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:45.930
She even spent as many as 11 years committed
to her role in "I Am Love," learning both

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:49.690
Russian and Italian to make her character
seem as realistic as possible.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:55.599
Swinton's name rarely makes it into the tabloids,
and even when it does, she isn't very interested

00:03:55.599 --> 00:04:00.610
in joining in the conversation, rarely feeling
the need to clarify details about her personal

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:02.230
and romantic life with the press.

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:06.120
In fact, it often takes her a while to hear
through the grapevine if there is a rumor

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.360
spreading about her in the first place.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:09.360
She joked,

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:12.720
"I'm playful at heart… and myth-making is
always fun."

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:17.590
For instance, when Swinton began dating artist
Sandro Kopp, the press speculated that she

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:21.560
had first gotten together with Kopp during
her relationship with her previous partner

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:24.150
of 14 years, playwright John Byrne.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:28.490
The gossip spread for years before Swinton
realized what was being said and had to come

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.950
forward to state that it was nothing but a
rumor.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:33.970
"I mean, this is really inappropriate."

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:39.000
If Swinton hasn't been filming blockbusters,
what has she been working on?

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.210
While fans of Swinton might have caught her
latest big-name projects, some of her recent

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:45.090
work has flown under the radar.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:50.400
In 2020, she lent her voice to the late composer
Jóhann Jóhannsson for his experimental film

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.280
"Last and First Men."

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:57.530
The movie explores a futuristic society in
which evolved humans face potential extinction,

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:01.350
and surreal monuments beam out messages into
the universe.

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:04.340
Swinton also worked on several short films
in 2020.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:09.060
She narrated "Story and the Writer," which
explored a man's efforts to write the perfect

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:10.060
screenplay.

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:14.750
In addition, she appeared in Pedro Almodóvar's
"The Human Voice," in which she played a woman

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:20.060
who notes the passing of time while she waits
for her ex-lover to come and pick up his suitcases.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:24.410
While the short was not widely viewed, it
did receive some glowing reviews.

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:27.630
As critic Ryan Rojas wrote in a review for
Cinemacy,

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:32.770
"Tilda Swinton commands every second of the
small screen in Pedro Almodóvar's beautifully

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:35.440
staged and winkingly meta new short film."

00:05:35.837 --> 00:05:40.980
In August, 2020, "The Personal History of
David Copperfield" was released.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:47.000
Armando Iannucci's comedic drama adapted Charles
Dickens' classic story for the modern age,

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.639
starring Dev Patel as the title character.

00:05:49.639 --> 00:05:54.500
Swinton portrayed Betsey Trotwood, David Copperfield's
eccentric great-aunt, who takes him in and

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.090
ends up financing his dream of becoming an
author.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.350
"Shoo, shoo, shoo!

00:05:58.350 --> 00:05:59.610
Off my lawn!

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:01.280
I'll box your ears!

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:02.540
Off you go!

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:04.810
This is a donkey-free zone!

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:06.250
Move it!"

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:10.560
Although critics held a generally positive
opinion of the film, that didn't prevent it

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:13.050
from being a flop at the box office.

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:17.060
The timing of its release certainly didn't
help, as the film arrived in theaters in the

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:22.280
midst of the COVID-19 pandemic, once a majority
of movie theaters had temporarily closed down

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:23.320
for safety reasons.

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:29.280
The pandemic disrupted the production schedule
for countless movies and TV shows.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:33.900
Many directors had to postpone shooting for
months on end, leaving lots of release dates

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:35.000
in limbo.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:39.260
While some studios have chosen to release
their new films through streaming services,

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:43.740
others have decided simply to delay their
releases, meaning audiences will have to wait

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:45.840
a little while longer to see them.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:50.220
That was the case for Swinton's highly anticipated
movie "The French Dispatch."

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:55.530
The Wes Anderson flick was originally slated
for a July 2020 release, likely at the Cannes

00:06:55.530 --> 00:06:56.530
Film Festival.

00:06:56.530 --> 00:07:00.850
However, the festival was canceled because
of the COVID-19 pandemic, and the tentative

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:06.713
release date was pushed to October 2020 - which
was again postponed until 2021.

00:07:06.713 --> 00:07:09.919
Swinton also has experience behind the camera.

00:07:09.919 --> 00:07:14.180
She is currently working on a documentary
about progressive education systems around

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:15.430
the world.

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:18.970
Swinton has been interested in creating schools
that encourage students to reach their full

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:23.980
potential for years, having co-founded the
Drumduan Upper School in Scotland, where her

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:25.490
own children attended.

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:30.520
The school does not require students to take
tests or even sit at desks most of the time,

00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:35.590
so it's likely that her documentary will focus
on unorthodox approaches to education.

00:07:35.590 --> 00:07:37.460
This won't be Swinton's first time directing.

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:42.660
In 2008, she was one of several directors
for the documentary "The New Ten Commandments,"

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:45.210
which explores human rights in Scotland.

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:49.780
And in 2016, she collaborated with several
other directors for the film "The Seasons

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:54.270
in Quincy: Four Portraits of John Berger,"
a tribute to the respected novelist.

00:07:55.669 --> 00:08:00.020
While it might seem like Swinton has been
laying low, she has been as busy as ever,

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:03.700
having been working on several upcoming projects
for some time.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:09.289
First up is her film "The Souvenir: Part II,"
a sequel to her 2019 film "The Souvenir" in

00:08:09.289 --> 00:08:12.800
which she stars alongside her daughter, Honor
Swinton Byrne.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:17.430
Her movie The Eternal Daughter is also anticipated
to release in 2021.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:21.919
Multiple upcoming Swinton films have yet to
gain official release dates, but fans can

00:08:21.919 --> 00:08:26.820
expect to see her in films such as the fantasy
epic "Three Thousand Years of Longing" and

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:28.730
the drama "Memoria."

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:33.399
She's also going to be voicing the Fairy with
Turquoise Hair in Guillermo del Toro's dark

00:08:33.399 --> 00:08:37.169
adaptation of the classic story "Pinocchio."

